{
  "program": "CORPT00C",
  "caseId": "case06",
  "description": "The WHEN MONTHLYI arm at :213-238 with CONFIRMI = 'Y', which is the headline case: it emits all seventeen eighty-byte records of 02 JOB-DATA-1 (:83-125) through the job-submission port, in emission order, each pinned byte for byte. On 9 August 2026 the arm composes 2026-08-01 from WS-CURDATE-YEAR, WS-CURDATE-MONTH and the literal '01' (:217-219), then moves 1 into the day, adds 1 to the month (:223-224) and subtracts a single day through FUNCTION DATE-OF-INTEGER of FUNCTION INTEGER-OF-DATE at :229-230 to reach 2026-08-31 - the last day of the current month. Both dates land in four distinct storage locations: PARM-START-DATE-1 in record 11's SYMNAMES line, PARM-END-DATE-1 in record 12's, and PARM-START-DATE-2 and PARM-END-DATE-2 in record 15, which is the DATEPARM record CBTRN03C reads. Record 17 is '/*EOF': :502 recognises it and :504 sets END-LOOP-YES, but :507 performs the write unconditionally afterwards, so the sentinel is itself emitted and the count is seventeen rather than sixteen. The write succeeds, so :445 finds the error flag off, INITIALIZE-ALL-FIELDS blanks the ten input items (:636-645), :448 moves DFHGREEN into ERRMSGC and :449-452 STRINGs WS-REPORT-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE with ' report submitted for printing ...' DELIMITED BY SIZE. Expected values are STATICALLY DERIVED by reading app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl, its copybooks, app/bms/CORPT00.bms and app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD - never captured from a COBOL run, which is impossible in this environment (risk R-A). Java has no transient data queue, so EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') at :517 is reproduced through an explicit job-submission port; the eighty-byte content is identical and the dataset key JOBS names the TDQUEUE(JOBS) that app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD:499-505 defines as RECORDSIZE(80) RECORDFORMAT(FIXED) BLOCKFORMAT(UNBLOCKED) DISPOSITION(MOD).",
